{
  "id": "within-subjects-factor",
  "term": "within-subjects factor",
  "definition": "A within-subjects factor is a variable in a study for which the same participants are tested under each of its conditions. In the example given, map orientation is a within-subjects factor because each orienteer experienced both the normal and rotated map conditions.",
